A||||3||RZURCTN||Two Scoops?||||6
Z||000000||RZURCTN||10-05-1999||11:47 PM||||I once saw a Fiero in AZ that had two scoops poking up over the roof.  Is there a kit for that or was somebody getting crazy with the fiberglas?  It was a few years ago, back in the day I owned my first Fiero and I don't know if it's my memory playing tricks on me or what.  At any rate, it looked like a good idea becase they came up from the removable panels and didn't seem to interfere with the operation of the deck lid.||||reg||6
Z||000001||TOM||10-06-1999||01:00 AM||||They look cool but if they are functional then they screw up the air flow. The fiero was designed so that the cooling air comes up from the bottom through the vents. If you try to force air down through the vents you will wind up with very little air flow in either direction.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Racer 1||10-06-1999||03:32 AM||||I totally agree with TOM. If you drive your fiero on the highway and stick your hand out the window back by the top of the roof you can fell the warm air coming out. Vacume affect by the rear window area. I also installed a fan in the pass side vent to cool the engine even more.||||reg||14
Z||000003||fiero56||10-06-1999||08:51 AM||||You don't even need to stick your hand out the window... all you need to do is feel how WARM the rear glass gets, especially on the highway, I never need my rear defroster. I heard about this before when I was talking with a guy who make his Fiero a convertable, he was talking about being able to feel engine heat on the back of his neck.||||reg||10
